{"description":"Measure the 'more context cliff' (H1 knee) and unit-budget priority (E1+E8): at what unit count does adding more CKOs degrade engineering task success, and does strata-priority truncation (constraints \u003e dependencies \u003e downstream noise) outperform naive tail truncation under a fixed budget. Provides the numeric basis for Finding 4 (Context Budget) and the budget guidance in fnd:llm-context-efficiency §4/§7.","investigationNotes":"Context: fnd:llm-context-efficiency Finding 1/4 claims sufficiency = focus + constraints (stratum \u003c focus) + 1-hop depends-on/derives-from (≈5-12 units) and that beyond this cliff more context hurts; budget recommendation is advisory at Agent Runtime with strata-priority. Both claims are HYPOTHESIS until measured.\n\nScope: controlled A/B on real eka-cli fixtures (testdata/conformance/valid, sto-login-email, plan-rilis-1-v1) and 3 cloned repos (eka-cli, eka-core, eka-mcp) with tasks of type fix/implement/review.\n\nE1 — full vs minimal: Variant A = eka context --depth dependency (with focus content) + full neighbor CKOs; Variant B = dependency --no-content (refs) + explicit eka get for focus only. E8 — strata-priority vs tail truncation: when over budget (16k cap), Variant A = naive tail truncation, Variant B = strata-priority keep (constraints \u003e dependencies \u003e downstream noise) + truncated:true flag.\n\nMetrics (both): tokens_transmitted, tokens_prefix_cached (if vendor header), task success rubric (correct files touched, constraint cited, state transition valid, no hallucinated requirement), LLM judge 'did constraint get used?'. Also record units count swept 2→20 to locate knee.\n\nDeliverable: knee at N units (or 'no clear knee'), strata-priority win/loss, and recommended budget defaults with evidence (FACT vs still HYPOTHESIS). Timebox 3-5 days. Transport: local run, no infra change; deterministic extraction, no LLM summarization of CKOs.","conclusion":""}